WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:03.220
The gearcase is the lower
unit under the water.

00:03.240 --> 00:07.590
Gears and bearings run in sealed oil.

00:08.260 --> 00:11.190
When you drain it, the
colour tells you something.

00:12.540 --> 00:14.510
Amber and clean is reassuring.

00:15.280 --> 00:19.490
Dark but oily may just be
used oil, but mention it.

00:19.760 --> 00:22.810
Milky or creamy means water is mixed in.

00:23.980 --> 00:26.190
Water and gear oil don't mix.

00:26.900 --> 00:30.970
They turn milky, and milky oil
doesn't lubricate properly.

00:31.780 --> 00:34.310
Water can rust bearings
and gears from inside.

00:35.820 --> 00:39.240
The main seals that keep the
lake out are at the prop shaft,

00:39.260 --> 00:45.390
driveshaft and shift shaft, plus
the drain and vent screw gaskets.

00:46.220 --> 00:48.350
A worn seal is one possibility.

00:48.960 --> 00:50.690
Only testing can tell.

00:52.060 --> 00:54.630
Don't just refill it and keep boating.

00:55.180 --> 01:00.520
Mercury warns water in the oil can
damage bearings and can freeze inside the

01:00.540 --> 01:04.390
gearcase. Stop running
it and get it looked at.

01:05.580 --> 01:09.130
We pressure and vacuum check
the case to find what's leaking,

01:09.520 --> 01:15.290
then inspect inside. We confirm the
scope before any repair is approved.

01:16.700 --> 01:23.920
Fill out the service request at hbwservice.ca,
with your serial number and a photo

01:23.940 --> 01:28.730
of the oil. Then drop off your
boat by trailer or by water.

01:29.560 --> 01:32.930
We're closed December
first to April first.
